 each member of one Galaxy\\ncollection and writes a combined table. Grouped-collection mode accepts repeated\\ngroup labels plus collections and writes a long table suitable for downstream\\ngroup comparison tools.</p>\\n<p>ZIP archive modes are convenience inputs for archive-heavy histories. They\\nextract local Galaxy ZIP datasets inside the job working directory, reject unsafe\\nmember paths such as absolute paths or <tt class=\\\"docutils literal\\\">..</tt> traversal, apply the same\\nsuffix/regular-expression filters, and then run the selected PhyKIT metric.\\nGalaxy-native collection mode remains the preferred route when users want to\\ninspect or reuse extracted archive members.</p>\\n<p>Collection outputs include:</p>\\n<ul class=\\\"simple\\\">\\n<li>a metrics table with group, file identifier, file name, metric, value, and\\nstatus columns;</li>\\n<li>a failed-files table with nonzero or unparsable PhyKIT runs; and</li>\\n<li>a summary table with total, selected, processed, failed, and skipped file\\ncounts per group.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>Use suffix or regular-expression filters when a collection contains mixed files,\\nfor example to process only <tt class=\\\"docutils literal\\\">.treefile</tt> members for tree metrics. In ZIP\\nmodes, leaving both filters blank processes every regular archive member and\\nwrites a warning to standard error.</p>\\n</div>\\n\",\n  \"help_format\": \"restructuredtext\",\n  \"hidden\": \"\",\n  \"hidden_versions\": [],\n  \"history_id\": \"bbd44e69cb8906b5547495f62686f8f4\",\n  \"icon\": null,\n  \"id\": \"toolshed.g2.bx.psu.edu/repos/goeckslab/phykit_metrics/phykit_metrics/0.2.0+galaxy0\",\n  \"inputs\": [\n    {\n      \"cases\": [\n        {\n          \"inputs\": [\n            {\n              \"cases\": [\n                {\n                  \"inputs\": [\n                    {\n                      \"argument\": null,\n                      \"default_value\": {\n                        \"values\": [\n               